### 3. Interactions Between Complexity and Size  
- combined_complexity: v(g) + ev(g) + iv(g) to represent aggregate structural complexity.  
- branch_size_interaction: branchCount * loc_branch_ratio (interaction of branch count and code size per branch).  

### 4. Halstead Signal-to-Noise Ratios  
- operator_balance: uniq_Op / uniq_Opnd (balance between unique operators and operands).  
- volume_difficulty_ratio: v / d (ease of comprehension per difficulty).  

### 5. Derived Feature Aggregations  
- scaled_effort: log(e) (log-transformed effort to reduce skew).  
- scaled_volume: log(v) (log-transformed Halstead volume for interpretability).  

### 6. Quality Ratios and Aggregations  
- comment_code_ratio: lOComment / (loc + 1e-5) (documentation emphasis).  
- blank_comment_balance: lOBlank / (lOComment + 1) (balance of blank vs. comment lines).  

### 7. Effort-Intelligence Indicators  
- effort_intelligence_diff: e - i (effort less intrinsic intelligence of code).  
- effort_intelligence_ratio: i / (e + 1e-5) (intelligence per unit effort).  

